This was Anderson's second stop-motion film, following Fantastic Mr.

16
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:58,000
The film is set in the fictional Japanese city of Megasaki where Mayor Kenji Kobayashi
has banished all dogs to Trash Island due to a canine influenza pandemic.

17
00:57:14,000 --> 00:57:20,000
Kobayashi's nephew Atari sets out to find his missing dog Spots with
the help of a group of dogs led by stray dog Chief.

18
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
Anderson started developing the film in October 2015 using stop-motion
animation, with a voice cast of Norton, Cranston and Balaban.

19
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:04,000
It draws inspiration from films by Akira Kurosawa and Hayao Miyazaki, as well as the stop-motion animated holiday
specials made by Rankin/Bass Productions, the 1982 animated film The Plague Dogs, and Disney's 101 Dalmatians.

20
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Production began in October 2016 at the 3 Mills Studios in East London.

21
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
By December 2016, Fox Searchlight Pictures acquired worldwide
distribution rights to the film, scheduling it for a 2018 release.

22
01:14:04,000 --> 01:14:10,000
It is the second animated film to be released by Fox
Searchlight, seventeen years after Waking Life in 2001.

23
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:32,000
It is the only  20th Century Fox Animation film to
be released by Fox Searchlight.

24
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
Isle of Dogs opened the 68th Berlin International Film Festival, where
Anderson was awarded the Silver Bear for Best Director.

25
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:16,000
It was given a limited release in the United States on March
23, 2018, and went on wide release on April 13.

26
01:27:32,000 --> 01:27:38,000
It grossed over $64 million worldwide, and received critical acclaim for its animation, story, musical
score, and deadpan humor, along with criticism for its portrayal of Japanese people and culture.

27
01:30:54,000 --> 01:31:00,000
The film received two nominations at the 91st Academy
Awards, for Best Animated Feature and Best Score.

28
01:34:16,000 --> 01:34:22,000
The film explores themes of island, japan, stop motion, dog, garbage dump.

29
01:37:38,000 --> 01:37:44,000
The tone is lighthearted.
